<title>FINLAND: Nokia says April handset promo routine.</title>
<headline>Nokia says April handset promo routine.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecommunications group Nokia Oy on Friday denied a press report suggesting it had dumped its mobile phones at factory prices in Finland a bid to secure market share over Swedish rival Ericsson.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for Nokia Mobile Phones said it had in April run a planned five-day promotional offer to mark the 10th anniversary of mobile phones in Finland, but denied suggestions in daily Kauppalehti that it was selling at factory prices.</p>
<p>&quot;It would be extremely expensive to buy more market share in an advanced market like this,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +3589 6805 0247, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
